Small-batch graph slot + graph-stage perf split - mm10, the fix the
2026-08-02 phase-split investigation demanded.

Speculative decoding alternates 1-token steps with small multi-token
verify passes. llama_context caches exactly ONE graph (gf_res_prev), so
every alternation re-pays CPU-side model.build_graph + sched_alloc
(measured: 0.12ms+0.13ms per pass on a desktop CPU, an estimated
10-20ms on SNP-throttled CVM vCPUs) AND destabilizes CUDA-graph capture
above it (allocations move every pass, so batched shapes never replay -
why the mm7 shape-keyed-capture experiment measured no gain). The mm9
fleet decomposition pinned 37-50ms of every verify inside llama_decode
with every other suspect measured innocent.

Change 1 (slot RING): ubatches of 2..8 tokens get a small LRU ring of
llm_graph_result + ggml_backend_sched pairs (GRAPH_SLOTS_ALT = 3),
keyed by EXACT token count and created lazily on first use
(non-speculative workloads never pay the extra compute buffer, which is
reserved at the slot's 16-token worst case, far below the primary's
prefill-sized arena). Each slot's own sched pool also hands CUDA-graph
capture a stable base address per shape for free. sched_active routes
the decode path (graph params, compute, output extraction) to the slot
that ran; both slots reset on memory updates. Local proof (0.8b,
alternating b1/b5 x100): build+alloc 0.123+0.125ms/pass -> 0.008+0.006,
greedy argmax chain BIT-IDENTICAL to the single-slot path.
LLAMA_GRAPH_SLOT_ALT=0 disables wholesale (config-only rollback).

Why a ring and not one slot (measured on the fleet, 2026-08-02): with a
single alt slot the CVM still paid gbuild 1.9-2.9ms + galloc 1.5-2.1ms
on EVERY verify, because a speculative round does not use one shape -
it interleaves verify(k+1), partial-accept re-feeds of 1..k tokens, and
(prompt-lookup) variable draft lengths, so the one-deep cache thrashed
exactly like the shared slot. The same fleet run proved the slot itself
engages (slot_state=1 on 110/110 verifies) and that CVM vCPUs build
graphs ~1000x slower than a desktop (0.008ms -> 2-3ms), which is why
this term is invisible locally and dominant in the enclave. Local
3-shape mix (b1/b2/b3 interleaved, CPU-only build): build+alloc
0.335+0.198ms/pass -> 0.008+0.005, argmax chain bit-identical.

Change 2 (instrumentation): llama_graph_perf(ctx, out[3]) - cumulative
read-and-clear micros of [build_graph, sched_alloc, set_inputs] inside
process_ubatch, the counters that named this bottleneck.

